node_modules/
# ...except the ones that are test data. WP21 S1 derives a module's package
# from the `node_modules/<name>` directory it sits in, so the fixture for two
# packages compiling together has to be laid out the way npm lays one out.
!tests/link/*/node_modules/
# ...including the two fixtures that nest a second `node_modules` inside the
# first on purpose: `tests/link/package_doubled`, where the walk cannot name a
# `node_modules` ancestor it reached by spelling `..` (WP21 S2, §10a), and
# `tests/link/package_symlink`, where one package is reached twice because
# neither compiler has a `realpath` (§10d).
!tests/link/*/node_modules/**/node_modules/
# ...and the one the cookbook needs, for the same reason: the bare-specifier
# entry (WP21 S2) is only a demonstration if the package it imports is laid out
# the way npm lays one out.
!docs/cookbook/node_modules/
dist/
build/
web/*.wasm
*.o
*.s
*.bc
a.out
.claude/worktrees/

# tests/link/no_main is a negative case: the compiler writes the IR beside the
# source before it reports the missing `main`, so every run of the link section
# leaves this behind. Two .ll files under tests/link ARE checked in
# (two_file/), so this names the one that leaks rather than ignoring the glob.
tests/link/no_main/main.ll
